[    1.9s]

== B. Proposition 1(a): preimage set and the tree recursion, checked on EVERY visited value ==
   values checked (3 does not divide m): 627078; children(m) from the forward map == formula preimages (k >= 1, one parity class, restricted to visited values): mismatches 0
   recursion w(m) = [m <= N] + sum over children w(a): failures 0
   multiples of 3 with a child (should be 0: multiples of 3 are leaves): 0
   nit: for m = 1 (mod 3) the note's set {(2^k m - 1)/3 : 2^k m = 1 mod 3} without 'k >= 1' would include k = 0, i.e. (m-1)/3, which is EVEN for every such m (224677 of them here), not an odd preimage; the set needs k >= 1
[    4.3s]

== C. Proposition 1(b): ancestor = (2^K m - c)/3^j with c = sum_{l=1}^{j} 3^(l-1) 2^(K_j - K_l); the note's bound 0 < c < 2^K ==
   3000 random odd starts, 137841 (start, orbit value) pairs: n = (2^K m_j - c)/3^j exact in every case
   the note's bound c < 2^K FAILS in 97032 of 137841 pairs (70.4%); first failure: start 421787, j = 3, inverse word begins [1, 2, 1], c = 23 vs 2^K = 16
   e.g. the inverse word (1, 1): ancestor (4m - 5)/9, c = 5 > 4 (m = 17: 17 <- 11 <- 7). Failures by the first two inverse letters: {(1, 1): 35440, (2, 1): 15800, (1, 2): 14816, (1, 3): 8279, (2, 2): 5501, (3, 1): 4391}
   correct bounds: c/2^K = sum_l 3^(l-1) 2^(-K_l) <= (3/2)^j - 1 (equality iff all k_l = 1): max observed ratio to that bound 1.0000; and c < 2^K m (positivity of the ancestor): max c/(2^K m) = 0.2018
   relative threshold shift c/(2^K m) = 1 - 3^j n/(2^K m) (the 'rounding'): median 1.15e-03, 90% 6.43e-02, 99% 1.56e-01, max 0.2018
   (the shift is a function of the word only, not of m; it is ~ sum over the path of 1/(3 a_l), large only through small intermediate values)
[    5.7s]

